diff --git a/docs/virtual-gamepad.md b/docs/virtual-gamepad.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4b58c1b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/virtual-gamepad.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Virtual gamepad
+
+Set **MiSTer controllers** to **Virtual gamepad for games** to expose the
+controllers plugged into the MiSTer as local gamepads while streaming. Each one
+is a uinput device with the kernel `xpad` driver's Xbox 360 identity
+(`045e:028e`) and layout, so SDL 2/3, Wine/Proton and Steam pick it up with
+their built-in mappings and no configuration.
+
+## Requirements
+
+* Write access to `/dev/uinput`. On NixOS: `hardware.uinput.enable = true;` and
+  add your user to the `uinput` group (log out and in again). Elsewhere, a udev
+  rule such as `KERNEL=="uinput", GROUP="uinput", MODE="0660"` does the same.
+* Enable **Joysticks: Digital** or **Analog** in Groovy_MiSTer's OSD before
+  starting the stream. Analog also forwards both sticks.
+
+## Mapping
+
+Map buttons in the MiSTer OSD by position, following RetroArch's
+`mister_joypad` convention:
+
+| Groovy input | Virtual pad |
+| --- | --- |
+| D-pad | D-pad (hat) |
+| Button 1 / 2 / 3 / 4 | A (bottom) / B (right) / X (left) / Y (top) |
+| Button 5 / 6 | Back / Start |
+| Button 7 / 8 | LB / RB |
+| Button 9 / 10 | LT / RT (fully pressed or released) |
+| Left / right analog | Left / right stick |
+
+Guide and stick clicks are advertised so button indices match the standard
+mapping, but Groovy has no inputs for them. With **Digital**, the sticks stay
+centred.
+
+## Behaviour
+
+Controller 1 appears when streaming starts; controller 2 appears on its first
+input, so games do not see a phantom second pad. Both are released and removed
+when streaming stops. Games that do not hotplug controllers should be started
+after the stream.
+
+Each Groovy snapshot becomes a single `write()` of evdev events on the input
+thread, which sleeps in `poll()` with no timeout and is woken by the packet
+itself. Unlike mpv mode there are no repeats, bindings or IPC in the path.
+Stale and duplicate snapshots are discarded using the same frame/order rule as
+the mpv mode; after a second without accepted input any snapshot is accepted,
+so a counter reset cannot freeze the pad.
